{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789680370,"nonce":"RQEZ8Y2Ay6Blw0qAx75RBjNXl48=","title":"flow sprint plan / groom / close: cross-project sprint planning","message":"Workflow 5. Not project- or epic-scoped: the candidate pool is every unstarted issue across the store, ranked by priority then age. `flow sprint plan` shows the pool against the next iteration's capacity (sum of estimates vs configured capacity), and takes JSON add/remove/reorder patches so an agent can propose an allocation and a human accepts it. `flow groom` walks the pool and applies inline patches (priority, estimate, assignee, split via `flow breakdown`). `flow sprint close` moves unfinished issues to the next iteration and records the carry-over so `flow report` can show it. Depends on the iteration decision (aba17f4) and the plumbing CLI (e8d6426).","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789680370,"nonce":"v93W9C3PtV6BehnKV2zA6Swq7og=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789680370,"nonce":"xvF/Ycx5hsrCsaYsh/fQ4ZSxono=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}